cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mera.jl in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Mera.jl: Analysis of astrophysical simulations in Julia"
abstract: >-
  Mera.jl is a Julia package for analysing astrophysical simulations. The released version reads
  RAMSES, a widely used code for astrophysical fluid dynamics. RAMSES writes gas on an adaptive mesh,
  refined where more detail is needed, together with gravity, radiation, particles, sinks and
  clumps. Mera.jl reads all of it into Julia tables and works on them: it selects regions, derives
  quantities in any unit, and makes projection maps from any angle, volume renderings, profiles,
  phase diagrams, clump catalogues, time series and movies.

  When a region, such as a sphere, cuts through a computational cell, Mera.jl can count only the
  share of the cell that lies inside, for example a third of its volume and mass, in every later
  sum, profile and map. This keeps results accurate, especially for small regions. Its numerical
  core is tested against exact solutions and against the reference values of the RAMSES test
  suite. Saved results record the snapshot, code and package versions behind them. The analysis is
  written for two kinds of table, cells on a grid and particles. With register_reader!, a reader
  for another astrophysical code fills these tables, and the analysis functions then work on its
  data. Readers for further codes, from grid codes to the moving mesh of AREPO, are in development.
type: software
